# Guest-side test/bench ELFs and generated reference tables: build products of
# source/translator/linux/tests/build_*.sh, not sources.
#
# These patterns keep ad-hoc/debug build products out of `git status`. They do
# NOT mean "guest ELFs are not committed": every guest a harness loads IS in the
# tree (force-added), because a fresh clone has no x86-64 cross toolchain and
# could otherwise run nothing. The consequence is a trap -- a new guest silently
# stays out of a clone -- and it has fired: bench_suite_x86_64 and its golden
# checksum table were ignored, so bench_run.py in any fresh clone/worktree ran
# 2 of 7 workloads and verified 0 checksums, without a word of complaint.
# If you add a guest a harness depends on, add a `!` line below AND make the
# harness fail loudly when it is missing (bench_run.py require_inputs()).
source/translator/linux/tests/*_x86_64
source/translator/linux/tests/*_host
source/translator/linux/tests/*.elf
source/translator/linux/tests/bench_*.txt
source/translator/linux/tests/bench_*.json
# Exceptions -- must stay last, git's last matching pattern wins.
!source/translator/linux/tests/bench_suite_x86_64
!source/translator/linux/tests/bench_suite_x86_64.native.txt
!source/translator/linux/tests/bench_suite_x86_64.baseline.txt
